<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan money market rates up in tight market.</title>
<headline>Pakistan money market rates up in tight market.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's money rates traded at higher levels on Wednesday in a cash-short market and dealers said they were unlikely to move much on Thursday.</p>
<p>Onvernight rates remained glued to the 20 percent mark throughout the day, a dealer at KASB &amp; Co said.</p>
<p>The dealer said one-week funds were also traded at 20 percent while three-month funds were offered at 18.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
